      "player": "Gem25F Truth",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "\"Aha! Just as I suspected! The 'inaction' was a setup! They've orchestrated a two-pronged attack: 'Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer' and 'Guide of Souls.' Not only that, but they've *conveniently* removed exactly enough threats from my board using their 'Solitude' and its manipulations, to leave me with only one viable blocker: 'Phelia, Exuberant Shepherd.' This is a classic bait-and-switch! They want me to block the less threatening 'Guide of Souls' to save a single life point, while that nefarious 'Ragavan' slips through, stealing treasures and setting them up for their next scheme!\n\
\n\
